# FIXED DEFECT, 2026-08-15 (panel 061), and it is the sibling of
# `fixedbugs-a-group-record-in-every-container` rather than the same case: that one
# is about two names, this one is about a walk.
#
# Symptom: an `extern` group whose members are ALL records emitted no `#include`
# at all, so its own field assertions named a type nothing had declared —
# `use of undeclared identifier 'Color'`, exit 2. Repairing that revealed the same
# defect one level on: the `#include` was written and the `-I` that finds the
# header was not, `fatal error: 'raylib.h' file not found`.
#
# Cause: `externs::headers` and `externs::named` both walk `program.functions`,
# which was every group member until 2026-08-15. A `record` lowers to no function,
# so no walk over the emitted program can see one; the answer is in the
# declarations. The premise that expired here was never written down — it was the
# **shape of the loop**, which is the form of CLAUDE.md §11's hazard that no
# comment convention can catch, because there is no comment.
#
# The case is deliberately a group with NO function in it. A group with one would
# have hidden both halves.

extern "raylib.h" package "raylib"
    record Color
        r: u8
        g: u8
        b: u8
        a: u8

function main()
    red = Color(r: 255, g: 0, b: 0, a: 255)
    print(red.r)
    print(red.a)
